---
export const prerender=true;import Base from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<Base><section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Engineering starts in your hands</p><h1>Big ideas.<br/>One finger<br/>at a time.</h1><p>Build, code and design a robotic hand, one finger at a time.</p><a class="button" href="/login">Log in to start learning →</a><p class="muted">For curious minds, ages 11 and up.</p></div><div class="hero-art"><svg viewBox="0 0 360 350" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative modular robotic hand"><g fill="var(--hh-part)" stroke="var(--hh-primary)" stroke-width="3"><rect x="90" y="180" width="180" height="120" rx="20"/>{[0,1,2,3].map(i=><g><rect x={92+i*45} y={40+Math.abs(i-1)*15} width="34" height="130" rx="12"/><circle cx={109+i*45} cy="125" r="7" fill="var(--hh-accent)"/><path d={`M${109+i*45} 170v25`}/></g>)}<rect x="270" y="155" width="37" height="100" rx="14" transform="rotate(30 270 155)"/></g><text x="180" y="250" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--hh-bg)" font-size="22">HW / 01</text></svg><p class="muted">HelpingHand · concept illustration</p></div></section><div class="grid">{[['01 / Build','Discover the mechanics','Explore how linkages turn movement into a curling finger.'],['02 / Code','Make your ideas move','Connect Arduino programming to a physical response.'],['03 / Design','Shape what comes next','Explore CAD parts and think through your own modifications.']].map(([n,t,d])=><article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">{n}</p><h2>{t}</h2><p>{d}</p></article>)}</div><section class="strip"><h2>Built for hands-on teaching.</h2><p>Teacher accounts include lesson notes, assessment criteria, and troubleshooting guidance alongside the student experience.</p><a href="/login">Explore with your teacher account →</a></section></Base>